  "notes": [
    "PROXY, NOT PIM. Protocol \u00a713.5: a software hog competes at the memory controller and in the caches and additionally takes GPU time slices or CPU cores; the two spin controls bound those side effects. The result is the sensitivity of the GPU work to lost bandwidth, not PIM interference.",
    "Background GB/s counts read + write, the same convention as E1's clone() row, and is reported alone and during the foreground run.",
    "Foreground pinned to cores 0-5, the CPU hog to 6-11; both recorded.",
    "tegrastats --logfile appends, so each log is deleted before its run (T001).",
    "E1 measured bandwidth varying run to run by up to 1.19x with clocks and temperature constant, which is the noise floor under every slowdown here."
  ]
